1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Your phone is an always-on computer. Why rent a server?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
phone-agent runs a Pi agent inside a Chrome tab on a phone.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,500
Launched from scratch: on the tailnet in two seconds.

4
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:18,000
The tab is a real Tailscale node, serving this chat page to my laptop.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:26,000
I ask what we did earlier. It remembers: the transcript lives in browser storage and survives restarts.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Every reply comes from DeepSeek on Tinfoil, over an attested, encrypted channel the phone verified itself.

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Now: show your golfed Fibonacci code, and run it again.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:47,000
The python tool is CPython in WebAssembly, sandboxed in a worker, sharing the agent's files.

9
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Output streams back to the laptop. The phone did all of it.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Pi, Tailscale and Pyodide in one tab, on a phone, controlled from anywhere on the tailnet. phone-agent.
